# Onion Engine task log

This Markdown file is the presentation-oriented record of completed work. New
completed tasks will be appended chronologically; it is not a replacement for
the technical progress log in `docs/agent/PROGRESS.md`.

## Completed

### M1 — Foundations

- Created the new repository layout, CMake presets and layered targets.
- Moved the 67 pure-core and 8 GPU tests into the new tree; retained all 98
  legacy tests.
- Added cross-platform CI: Linux, macOS arm64, macOS x86_64 targeting 12.0,
  and Windows; GPU tests run on Linux and are skipped where no runtime exists.
- Added platform data-directory precedence, durable append, atomic replace,
  sampling and key-store foundations.
- Added pinned dependency records, TLS-backend decision, canonical JSON,
  BLAKE2b-256 and Ed25519 golden vectors.
- Merged as M1 and tagged on the M1 merge commit.

### M2 — DeepSeek client checkpoint (in progress)

- Added a Python-standard-library fake DeepSeek server with healthy,
  rate-limited, truncating and slow-under-load scenarios.
- Added request recording that omits Authorization values, plus a portable
  smoke test.
- Implemented and tested the adaptive request limiter: 429/503 and timeout
  pressure halve its limit; healthy latency adds four; latency pressure holds;
  the configured ceiling and a floor of one are enforced.
- Changed latency baselining to the lowest successful 30-second median in the
  trailing hour (`35c2cf5`), so normal peak-hour latency can adapt gradually.
- Recorded and approved peak/off-peak pricing policy (`fd82539`): requests
  entirely within one window use that window's rate, crossing requests use the
  higher rate, and reservations always use the maximum rate.
- Stabilized the legacy pool-resize test on a dedicated branch using 20 ms fake
  replies; merged through PR #2 (`a76cdc1`) and into M2 (`9e8e636`). A final
  20-repeat local verification passed.
- CI checkpoint passed on all jobs for `35c2cf5`:
  https://github.com/youssefmahni/onion/actions/runs/38020639289
- Diagnosed the 1,000-request crash with ASan/UBSan: a worker held an iterator
  into its submission deque after releasing the mutex, allowing a concurrent
  submission to reallocate the deque. The worker now drains ready work while
  locked before handing it to libcurl.
- Switched the fake service to a daemon-threaded HTTP server with an accept
  queue of 2,048, and added a 1,000-concurrent-request load test.
- Added stable per-request curl storage, curl_multi_poll-only driving, Unix
  descriptor-limit raising with a 64-descriptor reserve, and 1,000-request
  closed-port/reset-connection regressions.
- Added Linux ASan/UBSan and TSan CI jobs. TSan then found and verified the
  fix for a second client construction-order race; the ASan job excludes the
  external POCL runtime so its leak reports cannot mask engine diagnostics.
- Verified the normal and ASan/UBSan 1,000-request benchmarks after both
  repairs: 1,149.14 req/s normal and 307.235 req/s instrumented, each with
  1,000 peak requests and no sanitizer report.
- Added benchmark reporting for latency percentiles, curl connection reuse,
  negotiated HTTP version, runtime HTTP/2 support, process thread count and
  budget reservation/settlement totals.
- Implemented timeout-safe accounting: a timed-out request consumes its full
  reservation as uncertain spend and is marked in the benchmark metering log.
- Added a 1,000-request accept-without-response regression: every request
  times out at one second and the circuit breaker opens after 20 failures.

## Next approved task

- Await owner approval before starting the M2 1,000-request benchmark or any
  real DeepSeek call.
